---
# Model of the figure 'bus-timing'. Edit this file; `kokeb-docs figures` draws it. Never edit the SVGs.
# Every number is a param with the datasheet section and page it comes from (`ref`, a name under refs here or in
# docs/hardware.yml); a number without one fails the build. Wave characters and keys: docs/figkit.md in ci-tools.
kind: timing
id: bus-timing
title: I2C timing of the address byte
kicker: On the bus
alt: >-
  I2C timing of the XMPL100: the start condition, the 7-bit address and the write bit, each held while SCL is high,
  and the acknowledge, with the start, setup and hold times of the datasheet.
reads: >-
  The two lanes are SCL and SDA, left to right in time. SDA falls while SCL is high (the start), the address bits
  follow, each stable while SCL is high, then the XMPL100 pulls SDA low for the acknowledge. The table under the lanes
  gives each interval with its datasheet value.
print: landscape
sources:
  - docs/model/bus-timing.timing.yml
bus: i2c
refs:
  i2c: {doc: ds, section: "6.2 I2C interface", page: 8}
  i2c-timing: {doc: ds, section: "6.3 I2C timing", page: 9}
signals:
  - {id: scl, label: SCL, wave: "11nnnnnnnnn1"}
  - {id: sda, label: SDA, wave: "10========0.", data: [A6, A5, A4, A3, A2, A1, A0, W]}
groups:
  - {from: 2, to: 9, label: "address 0x48 and W", ref: i2c}
  - {from: 10, to: 11, label: ACK}
params:
  - {id: thd-sta, symbol: tHD;STA, label: Hold time after a start condition, min: 0.6, unit: µs, ref: i2c-timing}
  - {id: tsu-dat, symbol: tSU;DAT, label: Data setup time, min: 100, unit: ns, ref: i2c-timing}
  - {id: fscl, symbol: fSCL, label: SCL clock frequency, max: 400, unit: kHz, ref: i2c}
marks:
  - {param: thd-sta, signal: sda, from: 1, to: 2}
  - {param: tsu-dat, signal: sda, from: 3, to: 3.5}
